PRICE, off the arms' own plans: 4 elasticity runs + 12 ratio runs = 10584 s of arms
  (a ratio run is its plan's wall line at duty 0.25 plus the alignment probe's
  seconds at full duty; an elasticity run is its plan's wall figure),
  tests/test_gpu.py ~25 s (38 tests) before them and the end suite ~3295 s
  (4992 tests) after them, at 0.66 s a test, session 4's pod rate,
  plus the preconditions ~480 s (the driver's own arm_minutes: thermal 3, calibrate 3, pin_probe-n64-g1 2 min),
  the probe check ~120 s (an allowance: it prints no plan), per-run compiles and
  weight copies ~720 s (60 s a ratio run, an allowance) and exfil ~300 s
  (an allowance) = 15524 s
  = 259 min; at $4.59/h about $19.79. Book 6 h.
  SEED SPACING at these prices, start to start, for every G: seed 0 to seed 1 ~102 min; seed 1 to seed 2 ~43 min.
  NOT in that figure: pod boot and checkout, any arm that REFUSES and is re-run,
  the seeds a V7 FAIL at seed 0 skips (less), and the follow-up that FAIL prints, run
  by hand after the chain: ~77 min a G, 3 seeds at --duty 0.1 at 1521 s each (R3's own
  plan at 0.1, 1461 s, plus 60 s) (more).
on the pod, first:
    git -C /workspace/moe-kernels checkout -- moe/bench/hardware/measured_nvidia_h200.yaml
    git -C /workspace/moe-kernels fetch origin && git -C /workspace/moe-kernels checkout -B r3-align origin/r3-align
    git -C /workspace/moe-kernels log -1 --format=%h    # must print the head that was pushed
then detached, APPENDING, so a --resume keeps the earlier passes' console:
    cd /workspace/moe-kernels && nohup setsid bash scripts/alpha_g_chain.sh >> /workspace/alpha_g_chain.out 2>&1 < /dev/null &
and watch:      tail -f /workspace/alpha_g_chain.out   (and $SESSION/CHAIN.tsv)
ledger    /workspace/session/alpha_g-nvidia_h200-20260923T162926Z/CHAIN-dryrun.tsv
read a pair on the laptop:  .venv/bin/python scripts/private_weight_reference.py --read RUN1/report.json --replicate-of RUN0/report.json
  (PAIRS-by-G.tsv already reads every seed of a G together that way; PAIRS-README.txt is the legend)
the ruler this session scored against is /workspace/moe-kernels/moe/bench/hardware/measured_nvidia_h200.yaml, TRACKED and dirty after
  calibrate: commit it with the results. copy off before releasing the pod:
    tar czf /workspace/exfil-alpha_g-nvidia_h200.tar.gz -C "/workspace/session" "alpha_g-nvidia_h200-20260923T162926Z" -C "/workspace/results" "gaps-nvidia_h200" -C "/workspace/moe-kernels" "moe/bench/hardware/measured_nvidia_h200.yaml" -C "/workspace/moe-kernels" results/calibration/<the run dir calibrate prints> -C "/workspace" "alpha_g_chain.out"
